<section id="faqs" class="faqs">
  <div class="faq-header">
    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <p>Everything you need to know about using <br> the DHMP AGBOR platform.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-container">
    <details class="faq-item" name="faq">
      <summary>Is it free to book an appointment on the platform?</summary>
      <div class="faq-content">
        <p>Yes, using the Health Connect platform to book your time slot is completely free. You will only pay your standard consultation or treatment fees when you arrive at the hospital.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" name="faq">
      <summary>What happens if I arrive late to my booked time?</summary>
      <div class="faq-content">
        <p>To keep the system fair for everyone, if you miss your scheduled window, your booking will expire and you will need to join the standard walk-in queue. However, you can easily cancel and reschedule in advance through the platform if you know you will be delayed.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" name="faq">
      <summary>Can I book an appointment for my child or elderly parent?</summary>
      <div class="faq-content">
        <p>Absolutely. Once you create your primary account, you can add dependents (like children or elderly family members) and manage their bookings directly from your dashboard.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item" name="faq">
      <summary>Do I need internet access at the hospital to check in?</summary>
      <div class="faq-content">
        <p>No. You only need the internet to book your appointment. Once booked, you will receive an SMS confirmation with your Booking ID, which you can simply show to the front desk when you arrive.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>









